          "code": "import numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import IsolationForest\nfrom sklearn.metrics import average_precision_score, roc_auc_score\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(2422)\n\n# Bangkitkan dataset 8D (N = 1.150) dengan 2 klaster normal + 60 anomali berkelompok (masking scenario!)\n# Saat psi terlalu besar (mis. 1024), sub-sampel memuat terlalu banyak anggota klaster anomali\n# sehingga butuh banyak potongan untuk mengisolasi mereka (efek masking); psi=128..256 mematahkan masking!\nn_norm = 1090\nn_anom = 60\nX_norm = np.vstack([\n    rng.normal(0.0, 1.0, size=(545, 8)),\n    rng.normal(3.8, 1.0, size=(545, 8)),\n])\n# Klaster anomali rapat (60 titik saling berdekatan di [7.5, -2.5, ...])\nanom_center = np.array([6.8, -2.8, 3.0, -2.5, 2.2, -2.0, 1.8, -1.8])\nX_anom = rng.normal(anom_center, 0.35, size=(n_anom, 8))\n\nX = np.vstack([X_norm, X_anom])\ny = np.array([0] * n_norm + [1] * n_anom)\n\nprint(\"=== 1. Eksperimen Ukuran Sub-Sampel psi (max_samples) Mengatasi Efek Masking (Liu et al. 2008) ===\")\nprint(\"max_samples (psi) | ROC-AUC | PR-AUC | Mean Score Norm | Mean Score Anom | Gap Skor\")\nprint(\"-\" * 85)\nfor psi in [32, 64, 128, 256, 512, 1024]:\n    iforest = IsolationForest(\n        n_estimators=100, max_samples=psi, contamination=\"auto\", random_state=42\n    ).fit(X)\n    # Di Scikit-Learn: score_samples(X) = -s(x, psi) dalam [-1, 0]; balik tanda agar skor anomali di [0, 1]\n    anom_score = -iforest.score_samples(X)\n    roc = float(roc_auc_score(y, anom_score))\n    pr = float(average_precision_score(y, anom_score))\n    m_norm = float(np.mean(anom_score[y == 0]))\n    m_anom = float(np.mean(anom_score[y == 1]))\n    print(f\"{psi:17d} | {roc:7.4f} | {pr:6.4f} | {m_norm:15.4f} | {m_anom:15.4f} | {m_anom - m_norm:+8.4f}\")\n\n# 2) Verifikasi Identitas API Scikit-Learn: decision_function(X) == score_samples(X) - offset_\nclf = IsolationForest(n_estimators=100, max_samples=256, contamination=0.05, random_state=42).fit(X)\ndiff_api = float(np.max(np.abs(clf.decision_function(X) - (clf.score_samples(X) - clf.offset_))))\npred_match = float(np.mean((clf.predict(X) == -1) == (clf.decision_function(X) < 0.0)))\nprint(\"\\n=== 2. Verifikasi Kontrak API sklearn.ensemble.IsolationForest ===\")\nprint(f\"offset_ terkalibrasi (contamination=0.05)            = {clf.offset_:.6f}\")\nprint(f\"Max |decision_function(X) - (score_samples - offset)| = {diff_api:.2e}\")\nprint(f\"Kesesuaian (predict == -1) vs (decision_function < 0) = {100.0 * pred_match:.1f}%\")",
          "expectedOutput": "=== 1. Eksperimen Ukuran Sub-Sampel psi (max_samples) Mengatasi Efek Masking (Liu et al. 2008) ===\nmax_samples (psi) | ROC-AUC | PR-AUC | Mean Score Norm | Mean Score Anom | Gap Skor\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n               32 |  1.0000 | 1.0000 |          0.4983 |          0.5903 |  +0.0919\n               64 |  0.9998 | 0.9967 |          0.4797 |          0.5976 |  +0.1178\n              128 |  0.9998 | 0.9961 |          0.4634 |          0.5744 |  +0.1110\n              256 |  0.9937 | 0.8622 |          0.4537 |          0.5465 |  +0.0927\n              512 |  0.9687 | 0.5209 |          0.4471 |          0.5220 |  +0.0750\n             1024 |  0.9534 | 0.4348 |          0.4308 |          0.5002 |  +0.0694\n\n=== 2. Verifikasi Kontrak API sklearn.ensemble.IsolationForest ===\noffset_ terkalibrasi (contamination=0.05)            = -0.536197\nMax |decision_function(X) - (score_samples - offset)| = 0.00e+00\nKesesuaian (predict == -1) vs (decision_function < 0) = 100.0%",
